PN,36506
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F365A1785750495
OL,3,CPrime Minister hails Bev Craig 'Queen
OL,4,Cof the North' as she becomes Mayor
OL,6,FMs Craig won 47.15% of votes in the
OL,7,Ffirst round, just short of the 50%
OL,8,Fneeded to win outright in the
OL,9,FSupplementary Vote (SV) system, so
OL,10,Fthere was a second round against
OL,11,FReform UK candidate Sian Astley, on
OL,12,F20.99%.
OL,14,FLabour gained 58,076 more votes when
OL,15,Fthe second preferences of the five
OL,16,Feliminated candidates were
OL,17,Fdistributed, with Reform getting
OL,18,F45,250, leaving Ms Craig on 309,525
OL,19,Fand Ms Astley on 157,178.
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G6/10
